Patient Dashboard - Coalition Technologies Skills Test

Overview

This project is a responsive healthcare dashboard created from the Adobe XD design provided in the Coalition Technologies skills assessment.

The dashboard displays patient information for **Jessica Taylor** using the provided patient dataset and visualizes diagnosis history using Chart.js.

--> Technologies Used

- HTML5
- CSS3
- JavaScript (ES6)
- Chart.js

--> Features

- Responsive healthcare dashboard
- Patient profile information
- Blood pressure line chart
- Respiratory rate card
- Temperature card
- Heart rate card
- Diagnostic list table
- Lab results section
- Clean and modular code structure

--> Project Structure

bash
patient-dashboard/
│
├── index.html
├── style.css
├── script.js
├── README.md
├── data/
│   └── patients.json
How to Run the Project
1. Open the Project Folder

Open the project folder in Visual Studio Code.

2. Install Live Server Extension

Install the Live Server extension in VS Code.

Extension:

Live Server by Ritwick Dey
3. Start the Project

Right click on:

index.html

Select:

Open with Live Server

The project will open in your browser.

Example:

http://127.0.0.1:5500/index.html
Important Notes
The project only displays data for Jessica Taylor as instructed in the assessment.
Chart visualization is implemented using Chart.js.
Patient data is loaded from a local JSON file.
No unnecessary UI interactions were implemented to stay aligned with assessment requirements.
Data Source

Patient data is stored locally in:

data/patients.json
